 "brief": "Level 2's map of 300 mm tiles (the Start tile, two 150 mm gaps, a T junction, a dead end, a crossing, the fixed 150 mm cube, the speed bump, the 20 degree ramps up and down with the raised straight between) with its tail re-laid through the evacuation zone: past the ramp down, a corner, a straight with two pieces of debris and a corner into the zone, 4 x 3 cells (inside 1160 x 860 mm) entered by its silver strip on the north side and left by its black strip on the west side to the Goal tile; 10.07 m of line. In the zone, 2 live victims (silver) and 1 dead victim (black), and the red and green evacuation points in two of its corners - the victims' places and the points' corners drawn for each run and never told to the program. The robot is G6.3's (the robot file rescue-line-open); a run on a changed robot is not this level's. It starts on the Start tile on the line, facing along it, moved up to 10 mm and turned up to 5 degrees. The RCJ referee judges the line as at levels 1 and 2 and counts each rescue: a live victim at rest wholly in the green point and untouched by the robot, the dead victim in the red point only after both live ones. A run ends once the program has ended and the robot has then stood still for 0.5 s, after 3 lacks of progress, or after 480 s. Score: (80 x the fraction of the line completed - leaving the zone and reaching the Goal included - + 20 if no lack of progress was called) x 1.4 for each rescue, / 2.744. Par 240 s (the record's; no term in the score). Pass: a mean of at least 60 over the 5 runs, and at least 4 of 5 stop on the Goal.",
